=== e15: FUTURAMA THEOREM = TWO DOUBLINGS ===

  Fresh elements needed to restore any permutation:

  n      trials   max_fresh    all≤2    avg_cycles   max_cycles
  10     500      1            True     1.98         4         [PASS]
  16     500      1            True     2.35         5         [PASS]
  4      500      1            True     1.09         2         [PASS]
  6      500      1            True     1.45         3         [PASS]
  8      500      1            True     1.69         3         [PASS]

  Cayley-Dickson analogy:
    Cross-term 1: -conj(d)*b  (first doubling: R→C)
    Cross-term 2: b*conj(c)   (second doubling: C→H or H→O)
    Analogy:      fresh X ↔ first cross-term (introduces the new dimension)
    Analogy:      fresh Y ↔ second cross-term (completes the involution)
    Two fresh elements in Futurama = two cross-terms in Cayley-Dickson. Both are the minimal addition needed to express the full inverse/restoration.
